A||||31||RossT||wheel offset (86-87gt) vs (88gt rear) ?s||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||12-12-2000||03:34 AM||||Ok, I just read this on online:<P>"Bolt pattern is five on 100mm circle for all years."<P>"If I read this correctly, this means that the 15x7 wheel on all four corners of the 86-87 GTs are different than the 15x7 wheel on the *back only* of the 88 WS6 cars." <BR>GOOD POINT! Yes, they are different. There is a three letter stamp on the wheel:<P>XBZ: 86-87 (35mm offset) <BR>XRS, XXJ: back of 88 (41mm offset) <P><BR>WHAT THE HECK DOES THAT MEAN????<P>What are the implications of using a 86-87gt 15X7 rims on the rear of an 88gt?  Would it fit, but just stick out or in 6mm??<P>Or would it not work at all??<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-12-2000||04:14 AM||||I remember reading that same article and assumed for many years that the '88 15x7 wheel had a different offset than the '86-'87.  That proved to be untrue.....all 15x7 Fiero lace wheels have the same offset (35mm, I believe).  The guy who wrote the article told me it was written in error.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||12-12-2000||04:28 AM||||Leave it to mrfiero!!! <P>Now why did they go to the 6 inch rim up front in 88??<P>Thanks Mike!<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 12-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-12-2000||05:22 AM||||I'm no suspension expert, but they went to the 6" wheel because the new suspension geometry permitted it.  I think it has something to do with a reduced scrub radius (??).  I'm sure someone here will know exactly why.<P>Technical stuff aside......it just looks better!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||12-12-2000||11:07 AM||||The spacing from hub to hub on the front of the 88s was increased. If you put the 7" wheels on the front of an 88, they stick out quite a bit. Look a bit strange, IMHO. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||12-12-2000||12:51 PM||||ok... so do the '88 rims fit the '87,86,85, and 84 cars?<P>i don't understand this "offset" stuff.<P>hoop||||reg||5
Z||000006||Raydar||12-12-2000||02:07 PM||||Yes. All of the 15x7 wheels are the same casting. All years. Will fit any year Fiero. <BR>The 15x7s, IMHO, look funny on the <I>front</I> of an 88, though. Poke out too far.<BR>I have seen the 15x6, "88 only" front wheels on the front of an 86 SE. Didn't look bad. <BR>Not sure if the 88 14x6 wheels are the same as other years or not. 22P book lists a different part#. Anybody?<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-12-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000007||RossT||12-12-2000||05:26 PM||||Very informative Raydar, thanks.  Anyone else have comments about using 86-87 gt rims on an 88 gt (5x7 on front). I was thinking of refinishing a set of pre 88's to use  on my  88.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||Xtreme Fiero's||12-12-2000||05:53 PM||||I was told by a local Pontiac dealer that 88's got 6" rims up front to help the car "Push" at the limit to reduce oversteer. makes sence to me. anyone else hear the same thing?||||reg||1
Z||000009||88formula||12-12-2000||06:54 PM||||There is one easy way to find out if there is a difference, just measure an 87 and compare it to an 88 wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||12-12-2000||06:59 PM||||My rear 88 15*7 wheel measures 5-1/8 inches offset. I put a straight edge on the back of the wheel and measured to the mounting flange.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||12-12-2000||07:47 PM||||I have seen an 88 coupe before with 87 GT wheels.  Not pretty.  It stuck out way too far.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000012||RossT||12-12-2000||11:30 PM||||so an 87gt with 15X7 stock gt rim on front looks ok....<P>but an 88gt with 15X7 (from 87gt) stock rim on front sticks out to far? <P>Shouldn't the 88 look just like the 87 with the 7 inch rim?  Or is the upgrade in suspension make it different?<P>thanks again..||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||12-13-2000||09:41 AM||||Ross,<BR>The redesigned front suspension makes the 88 hub faces stick out farther from the center of the car. I'm guessing 1/2" - 1" on each side. I didn't believe it either, until I saw an 88 GT with with a 15x7 wheel on the front. <BR>I wanted to do exactly the same thing that you're trying to do.  <BR>I'll try to post a link to a pic. <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-13-2000).]||||reg||1
